<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ui version="4.0">
 <class>FormDialogPackage</class>
 <widget class="QDialog" name="FormDialogPackage">
  <property name="windowTitle">
   <string>Package</string>
  </property>
  <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="verticalLayout">
   <item>
    <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout">
     <item row="1" column="5">
      <widget class="QComboBox" name="interruptOverride">
       <property name="whatsThis">
        <string>&lt;p&gt;NPC AI can be interrupted by four events:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
   &lt;li&gt;Entering combat&lt;/li&gt;
   &lt;li&gt;Warning the player to leave an area that they're guarding (via a Guard package)&lt;/li&gt;
   &lt;li&gt;Finding a dead body&lt;/li&gt;
   &lt;li&gt;Spectating combat without being involved in it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Typically, NPCs who experience these events will suspend execution of their current AI package and begin executing special hardcoded behaviors. However, it's possible to instead have them execute an alternate AI package. The way to do this is by flagging the alternate AI package as an Interrupt Override of the desired type, adding it to a FormList, and then setting that FormList as the &quot;override package list&quot; (of the appropriate type) for the actor.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This drop-down box, then, is where you flag an AI package as an Interrupt Override.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Note that if you take a package that &lt;em&gt;isn't&lt;/em&gt; set as an Interrupt Override here, and try to &lt;em&gt;use&lt;/em&gt; it as an Interrupt Override, the game may crash.&lt;/p&gt;</string>
       </property>
       <item>
        <property name="text">
         <string>None</string>
        </property>
       </item>
       <item>
        <property name="text">
         <string>Combat</string>
        </property>
       </item>
       <item>
        <property name="text">
         <string>GuardWarn</string>
        </property>
       </item>
       <item>
        <property name="text">
         <string>ObserveCombat</string>
        </property>
       </item>
       <item>
        <property name="text">
         <string>Spectator</string>
        </property>
       </item>
      </widget>
     </item>
     <item row="0" column="1" colspan="4">
      <widget class="QLineEdit" name="editorID"/>
     </item>
     <item row="1" column="0">
      <widget class="QLabel" name="label_2">
       <property name="text">
        <string>Owning Quest:</string>
       </property>
       <property name="buddy">
        <cstring>owningQuest</cstring>
       </property>
      </widget>
     </item>
     <item row="0" column="5">
      <widget class="QCheckBox" name="flagIsTemplate">
       <property name="whatsThis">
        <string>&lt;p&gt;A &lt;dfn&gt;package template&lt;/dfn&gt; can define a procedure tree that can be reused by other packages, along with blanks that those packages can fill in to tweak the procedures. However, package templates can't define schedules, Papyrus data, or idle animation overrides.&lt;/p&gt;</string>
       </property>
       <property name="text">
        <string>Is Template</string>
       </property>
      </widget>
     </item>
     <item row="1" column="4">
      <widget class="QLabel" name="label_3">
       <property name="text">
        <string>Interrupt Override:</string>
       </property>
       <property name="buddy">
        <cstring>interruptOverride</cstring>
       </property>
      </widget>
     </item>
     <item row="0" column="0">
